## A Colorful Problem: Galaxy RG Corp's Undeclared Additives

This week's standout story revolves around Galaxy RG Corp, which has managed to single-handedly flood the recall reports with eleven separate items of confectionery containing undeclared artificial colors. Yellow #5, Yellow #6, and Red #40 appear to be the unwelcome guests in these products, which range from guava rolls to strawberry cheesecakes.

While undeclared allergens are a frequent flyer in recall announcements, the revelation of unlabeled synthetic colorants raises concern. Consumers might not be as vigilant about color additives as they are about peanuts or gluten, yet the health ramifications can be just as dire for those sensitive to these compounds. Considering Galaxy RG Corp's roster of repeat offenses, it might be time for them to reassess their labeling practices and quality checks.

## Supplements Under Fire

Total Nutrition Inc has also found itself in hot water this week. Their Ultrapotent Complete Green Superfood Moringa Capsules were yanked from shelves due to potential salmonella contamination. This Class I recall, the most severe classification, underscores a breach in manufacturing safety protocols that could jeopardize consumer health.

## A Broader Look at 2026

This year's recall statistics so far paint a troubling picture: 577 recalls in total, with a significant chunk (30%) falling under the Class I category--life-threatening issues. Notably, there have been 176 Class I recalls while Class II recalls make up the majority at 361, indicating a widespread issue with labeling and quality oversight.

## Conclusion

As food recalls continue to pile up, the responsibility to scrutinize our purchases grows heavier. Brands like Galaxy RG Corp, with repeated lapses, erode consumer trust and highlight gaps in regulation and enforcement. The question remains: how many more alerts will we need before systemic change occurs?

Among the recent recalls, SENSORY SUPPLEMENT LLC and Total Nutrition Inc also stand out for their quality issues. The former's premature lipid oxidation and the latter's salmonella contamination are reminders that vigilance is necessary, even for supplement products often perceived as inherently safe.

### Items Recalled This Week

1. Galaxy RG Corp: Marquesita de Chocolate y Vainilla, Rollitos de Guava, Rollitos de DulceLeche, Cheesecake de Fresa, Tiramisu, Marquesita de Mango, Cake de Fresa y Chocolate, Cake de Mango, Cheesecake de Guava.
2. Total Nutrition Inc: TNVitamins Ultrapotent Complete Green Superfood Moringa Capsules and Doctor's Pride Complete Green Superfood Ultra Potent Moringa.
3. Refresqueria Estrella Inc.: ESTRELLA Bebida de Parcha.

### Brands on Notice

Galaxy RG Corp's frequent recalls are becoming unsettling, with Wellnov Supplements LLC and Diva Fam Inc also sporting high recall counts this year. Perhaps it's time to start reading labels with Sherlock-like scrutiny.
